# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Distributed data backend: Redis.
#
# Selected by the multi-node E2E runners with `--middleware redis`, which also starts the `redis` service from
# docker/redis.yml. With this backend no Hazelcast instance is created at all, so the run exercises the Redis
# implementations of every distributed structure.
#
# `spring.data.redis.client-name` is deliberately NOT set here: it must be unique per node and is therefore set by the
# runner scripts, which know the node number. It also doubles as the node identity the Redis provider reports, so two
# nodes sharing it would look like one node to the build agent cleanup.
#
# The host differs between the two runners (container DNS name vs. published port on the host) and is likewise set by
# the runner, so this file only carries what both have in common.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTEMIS_DISTRIBUTEDDATA_PROVIDER="Redis"
SPRING_DATA_REDIS_PORT="6379"
